Z||000000||fropuff||06-21-2001||12:49 AM||||Hey guys.  I'm wondering if one of you will be my troubleshooter quickly.  Okay, here goes: when I'm driving my Fiero (86 GT-matters?  Probably not), the left rear suspension squeaks like a b*tch.  It's probably some suspension component.  It's when I go over a bump.  When the road's rough, it goes all the time.  It sounds kinda like a mouse, like a chirping sound.  To make it clearer, when I drive over a bump, only the left rear suspension area sqeaks, chirps, etc.  Not a grind.  What can this be?  Sorry for being so vague.  If there's any questions relating to the problem, I'll try to answer them.  Thanks for any help.  Again, sorry for the retardedness.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-21-2001||01:42 AM||||Drive over bumps and when you hear it squeek, lightly apply the brakes. If it goes away it could be low brakes pads. The other things it could be is a bad bushing or a bad strut. On the strut you can pull the tire off and see if it is leaking fluid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||06-21-2001||08:59 AM||||Well, the brake pads are new; just replaced them 100 miles ago.  Unless I forked something up...  It probably is just a bad bushing or strut; I'll have to check.  So when the strut is bad, it leaks stuff out?  Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-21-2001||09:17 AM||||Get a can of WD40 and spray every joint. Or if you want to see where the exact culprit is do one joint and drive until you get the little bugger||||reg||14
Z||000004||87GTZ34||06-21-2001||10:12 AM||||It is most probably the strut but check the mount for the control arm while your into it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mr.Frosty||06-21-2001||10:24 AM||||I had this problem on my 88 Formula.It was a bushing on the rear sway bar.It was OEM black rubber and dried out.Get urethane all around.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
